!Experimental cmavo used by one person and generally understood

* ((mu'ei)) - used in ((Flatland)). It has also been used by other people, but mostly in the context of discussing what word to use for "if".

* ((xa'o))
** ''".i .uiru'e .a'ucu'i ku'i pe'i mi jinga ki'u le du'u xy. xa'o darlu"'' - said by ((xod)) in [http://groups.yahoo.com/group/lojban/message/8389
**] a few other uses by ((xod))

* ((xo'a)) --see [http://nuzban.wiw.org/wiki/index.php?JCB,] which is taken from the egroups list (at the time of the First Digger's '' co'a lenku margu'').
** .uanai.  "cool mercury"?? (See ((LojbanSlang)).)
*** Also ((ctatanru|here)).

* a'oe - ((kreig.daniyl.)) [http://groups.yahoo.com/group/lojban/message/8696|suggested] using an extra letter to clarify which sense of a'o was meant, and has used a'oe (event is hoped for and not asserted) ((Borrowing from Loglan|here)), ((if|here)), ((foo|here)), and on his homepage.
** ''oe'' isn't even a Lojban dipthong! (It would be confused with ''ue''.) How about ''a'oi''? --((rab.spir))
*** I had been pronouncing it as three syllables, like ''a'o,e'' except that cmavo don't have commas in them. But I will now use a'o'e instead, and I will fix all my uses of it.

*  ((goi'a)) - on my homepage. ((kreig.daniyl.))
** Given the understanding of ''goi'' now, should this be moved to Obsolete?

* ((ba'oi)) - Used by ((And)) in ((Round Two)) of the ((Broken Phone)) game.

